From a8f49da8fa44b6c451521d2f8426e3760f2febe0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 14:59:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Size-independent orphan cleanup, volume on cleaned roots,
 hook in figures

- Orphan cleanup: connectivity computed with sorted voxel keys instead of a
  KD-tree over all voxel pairs (same connected components, linear memory);
  the cleanup now runs on every sample and ORPHAN_MAX_VOX is removed
- VRT and SRT are measured on the mask voxels attached to the cleaned roots
  (nearest skeleton voxel), so hypocotyl, sheets and orphans are excluded
  and IC and SRL combine consistent quantities
- Pivot tip correction factored into cut_pivot_hook, used by the traits and
  the review figure; the cut hook is drawn as a separate trace
- Collar layer, hypocotyl angle, climb fraction, high branch margin and
  hook cut exposed as keyword arguments (defaults unchanged)
- tools/sensitivity.py: one-at-a-time sensitivity analysis of the thresholds
- tests/test_components.py: connectivity, hook cut and root mask tests
- Docs updated accordingly

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PmEM2KX1GoYpy4haNdkRoA
